<article class="env-proposition" id="08836D">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08836D">Proposition <span data-tag="08836D">1.2.2.3</span>.</a> Let $\calC $ be an $\infty $-category containing a pair of objects $x$ and $y$. The simplicial set $\Hom ^{\rght }_{\calC }(x,y)$ is a Kan complex. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      It is immediate from the definition that if $\calC $ is a $\infty $-category, then $M=\Hom ^{\rght }_{\calC }(x,y)$ satisfies the Kan extension condition for every horn inclusion $\Lambda ^ n_ i \subseteq \Delta ^ n$ where $0 < i \leq n$. This implies that $M$ is a Kan complex (Proposition <a href="/tag/9FABF2" data-tag="9FABF2">1.2.5.1</a>). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>